    "narrative": "The standout play for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is **Mickey Moniak** (75.75), who benefits from an optimal intersection of a favorable park factor (+14%) and a soft matchup against Roki Sasaki. His score is further buoyed by a slow-delivery pitcher that boosts his stolen base potential by 2%, keeping him as a priority start to chase our scarcity targets. **Isaac Paredes** (68.00) also presents as a high-floor, high-ceiling play against Walbert Ure\u00f1a; he maximizes his production through a significant platoon advantage (+9%) and a favorable SP skill rating (+12%), making him an anchor for the infield today.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup optimizer was the exclusion of **Austin Riley** (56.58). While he sits just outside our preferred threshold of 60 for an \"Elite\" start, his efficiency against Taj Bradley was strong, bolstered by a 2% boost from a slow pitcher that keeps the door open for stolen base opportunities. Ultimately, the optimizer prioritized the higher projected efficiency and order-dependent upside of **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Seiya Suzuki**. Risk management remains critical today as the vast majority of our roster\u2014including **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, **Jose Caballero**, **Max Muncy**, **Brice Turang**, **Griffin Conine**, **Corbin Carroll**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Vinnie Pasquantino**\u2014are currently based on pending lineups. Users should monitor late-afternoon announcements, particularly for **Corbin Carroll**, whose score takes a notable hit against the lefty Payton Tolle; his inclusion relies on the defensive value of his sprint speed relative to the limited alternatives on the bench.",
